course: dictionary
lesson: 11371
title: Ablaze
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Ablaze is a describing word, and it often comes after a verb, as in «The barn was ablaze.» It means burning strongly, on fire. Check the words around it to be sure which meaning fits.
explain: Ablaze can also mean shining very brightly, or full of colour. In «The sky was ablaze with fireworks», nothing is on fire. The sky is full of bright light, and the word fireworks is your clue.
explain: Ablaze can show strong feeling too: «Her eyes were ablaze with anger.» Her eyes are not really burning. They show she is very angry. When you see ablaze with, ask yourself: is it fire, light or feeling?
fact: Ablaze means burning strongly, on fire.
fact: Ablaze with light or colour means shining very brightly, as in «The garden was ablaze with colour in June.»
fact: Ablaze with a feeling means full of strong feeling, such as anger or joy.
fact: If a building is ablaze, get out, stay out and call the fire brigade.
fact: «Set ablaze» means made to catch fire, and «ablaze with» is a useful phrase to remember.
exercise: «The old shed was ablaze before the firefighters arrived.» What does ablaze mean here? | Covered in snow | Clean and freshly painted | *Burning strongly, on fire | Cold and empty
exercise: «The street was ablaze with Christmas lights.» What does ablaze with mean here? | *Shining very brightly | Full of rain | Very dark and quiet | Burning and dangerous
exercise: «Her eyes were ablaze with joy when she opened the present.» What does this show? | Her eyes were on fire | She was asleep | *She was full of strong feeling | She was bored
test: «The kitchen was set ablaze by a pan of hot oil.» What does set ablaze mean? | Painted bright red | Cleaned until shiny | *Made to catch fire | Made very cold
test: «The night sky was ablaze with stars.» What does ablaze mean here? | Burning and hot | Falling quickly | Covered in clouds | *Shining very brightly
exam: «The hills were ablaze with autumn colours.» Which meaning fits best? | Full of anger | Burning in a fire | Cold and grey | *Shining with bright colour
